3;3(3):200–205. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Asadi-Lari M, Madjd Z, Goushegir S. Gaps in the provision of spiritual care for terminally ill patients in Islamic societies—a systematic review. Adv Palliat Med . 2008;7(2):73–80. [ Google Scholar ] 30. Al-Mutair AS, Plummer V, Clerehan R, et al. Needs and experiences of intensive care patients’ families: a Saudi qualitative study. Nurs Crit Care . 2014;19(3):135–144. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 31. Nasir LS, Abdul-Haq AK. Caring for Arab patients: a biopsychosocial approach . Oxford, UK: Radcliffe Publishing; 2008. [ Google Scholar ] 32. Wenger NS, Lynn J, Oye RK, et al. Withholding versus withdrawing life-sustaining treatment: patient factors and documentation associated with dialysis decisions. J Am Geriatr Soc . 2000;48(5 Suppl):S75–83. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Lazenby S, Edwards A, Samuriwo R, et al. End-of-life care decisions for haemodialysis patients - ‘We only tend to have that discussion with them when they start deteriorating’. Health expect . 2017;20(2):260–273. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Puntillo KA, McAdam JL. Communication between physicians and nurses as a target for improving end-of-life care in the intensive care unit: challenges and opportunities for moving forward. Crit Care Med . 2006;34(11 Suppl):S332–340. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Luckett T, Sellars M, Tieman J, et al. Advance care planning for adults with CKD: a systematic integrative review. Am J Kidney Dis . 2014;63(5):761–770. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Morton RL, Kurella Tamura M, Coast J, et al. Supportive Care: Economic Considerations in Advanced Kidney Disease. Clin journal Am Soc Nephrol . 2016. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. Chandna SM, Da Silva-Gane M, Marshall C, et al. Survival of elderly patients with stage 5 CKD: comparison of conservative management and renal replacement ther