majo.20210091. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Brandt J, Shearer B, Morgan SG. Prescription drug coverage in Canada: a review of the economic, policy and political considerations for universal pharmacare. J Pharm Policy Pract. 2018;11:28. doi: 10.1186/s40545-018-0154-x. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Moorkens E, Vulto AG, Kent J, et al. A look at the history of biosimilar adoption: characteristics of early and late adopters of infliximab and etanercept biosimilars in subregions of England, Scotland and Wales - a mixed methods study. BioDrugs Clin Immunother Biopharm Gene Ther. 2021;35:75–87. doi: 10.1007/s40259-020-00456-5. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. McClean AR, Law MR, Harrison M, et al. Uptake of biosimilar drugs in Canada: analysis of provincial policies and usage data. CMAJ Can Med Assoc J J Assoc Medicale Can. 2022;194:E556–E560. doi: 10.1503/cmaj.211478. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Teeple A, Ellis LA, Huff L, et al. Physician attitudes about non-medical switching to biosimilars: results from an online physician survey in the United States. Curr Med Res Opin. 2019;35:611–617. doi: 10.1080/03007995.2019.1571296. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Chew C, Aguiar M, Bansback N, et al. Patient perspectives on the British Columbia biosimilars initiative: a qualitative descriptive study. Rheumatol Int. 2022;42:1831–1842. doi: 10.1007/s00296-021-04874-8. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. Bessette L, Lebovic G, Millson B, et al. Impact of the adalimumab patient support program on clinical outcomes in ankylosing spondylitis: results from the COMPANION study. Rheumatol Ther. 2018;5:75–85. doi: 10.1007/s40744-018-0109-3. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in t